'''4.''' Preparatory measure or negotiation; previous disposition or plan; preparation: commonly in the plural: as, we have made ''arrangements'' for a journey.
{{smaller block|Previous to his departure he made all due ''arrangements'' with the holy fraternity of the convent for the funeral solemnities of his friend. {{right|''Irving'', Sketch-Book, p. 198.}}}}
{{smaller block|An elaborate ''arrangement'' was entered into at the same time by the Allied Powers, to provide for a succession to Parma in the event of the sovereign dying childless.
